caption: The Living Truth
tradition-component: the-living-truth

The Revelator treats a stable conjunction as something that can temporarily grow another psychic function. While expressing a Revelation, the character may use Wild Ability to graft one otherwise legal Advanced Psi ability from either Revelator Power onto a purchased Conjunction Ability.

The grafted ability must be mechanically integrated into the host conjunction using Linked, Follow-Up, Accessibility, or another legal construction that makes it part of that use. It cannot operate separately during the graft. Build and price the temporary component normally for purposes of Wild Ability, and obey the normal Wild Talent and Wild Ability limits. The purchased host conjunction remains unchanged after the temporary manifestation ends.

At Mastery, Living Truth becomes Origin-facing. The grafted temporary component may instead be governed by any Psi or Super Power Talent the character legitimately possesses. Use the maximum access band and caps the character already has for that Talent or Power; Revelator does not improve an unrelated Power's access. For a Super component, this is an explicit Eldritch exception to the Psi-origin restriction on the Revelator's Wild Ability, but only for a graft onto a purchased Revelator Conjunction while expressing a Revelation. It grants no general ability to use Psi Wild Talent to improvise Super powers.
